    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;2.02</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Differential diagnosis of conjunctival blue naevus</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Hardeep Singh Mudhar",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 769px; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.562px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 377.812px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"51%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Main histological features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.5px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"26%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">References</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.562px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conventional conjunctival blue naevus</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 377.812px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"51%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Heavily pigmented bland spindle/dendritic/stellate melanocytic cells in the conjunctival substantia propria; melanocytic cells show slender, branching networks of dendritic processes, frequently associated with melanophages and stromal fibrosis; no cellular atypia is present; mitotic figures are absent; no associated junctional melanocytic proliferation or entrapped epithelial cysts, except in combined or collision lesions</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.5px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"26%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.3.1.4&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Blue naevus of the conjunctiva</span></em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{29551421;2657539}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.562px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cellular blue naevus</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 377.812px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"51%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Dense aggregates of cytologically bland pigmented spindle cells and/or ovoid variably pigmented melanocytic cells, arranged as sheets or fascicles, surrounded by collagen and melanophages, frequently set in a background of common blue naevus</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.5px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"26%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.3.1.4&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Blue naevus of the conjunctiva</span></em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{29551421;2657539}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.562px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pigmented conventional melanocytic naevus</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 377.812px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"51%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Do not tend to feature spindle/dendritic/stellate melanocytic cells and commonly contain epithelial cysts</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.5px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"26%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.3.1.2&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Junctional, compound, and subepithelial conjunctival naevi</span></em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{29551421;2657539}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.562px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Invasive conjunctival melanoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 377.812px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"51%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cytologically atypical melanocytic cells in the substantia propria with or without mitotic figures; conjunctival melanocytic intraepithelial lesion may be present</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.5px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"26%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.3.2.2&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival melanoma</span></em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{29551421;2657539}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.562px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Malignant blue naevus</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 377.812px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"51%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Less pigmented, cytologically atypical, mitotically active melanocytic cells in the context of a blue naevus background</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.5px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"26%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{11074819;29551421;2657539}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.562px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Extrascleral extension of uveal melanoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 377.812px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"51%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Will contaminate the deep aspect of the biopsy with a broad base and will comprise atypical spindle/epithelioid melanocytic cells with prominent nucleoli, with or without mitotic figures, in the setting of an intraocular uveal mass</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.5px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"26%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.2.2.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Choroidal and ciliary body melanomas</span></em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{29551421;2657539}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.562px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pigmented foreign bodies</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 377.812px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"51%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Intrinsically acellular although may excite a foreign body histiocytic response mimicking melanophages; examples include minerals, mascara, graphite, and adrenaline pigment</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.5px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"26%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{25104745;15829815;3836032;14060094}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
